The mogilefs module turns nginx into a MogileFS client: it asks a tracker
where a key lives and hands the answer to proxy_pass, so nginx serves the
file straight from the storage node that holds it.  Writing and deleting
through the tracker work as well, and the copies a tracker names beyond
the first are available as variables, so a configuration can fall back to
another storage node itself.

This port only installs the module sources.  The module itself is built by
the nginx ports when their HTTP_MOGILEFS option is enabled.
